  ('13ba7aff-a22f-5216-9116-1660676828bd', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant — Operational Authorization', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'The Fire Control Sergeant is the Developmental position at this grade. The focus at this level is on the operational unit, where Sergeants build on their foundational knowledge to become technical and tactical experts while improving their leadership abilities. This dedicated focus is essential for achieving complete mastery of their core competencies.', '80d3bcc03ec06bfd563c91e1a5e16a13dfa61cf8711aa142e11d0c0ca404dec0', 25, 25, null, 81, null, null, false, null),
  ('a699e200-defb-5aac-8235-be2e46fcbb4f', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'self_development', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Sergeants who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Key', 'a946340848989ddd2a4ac4056d37dfeeab3cd95d164911b3616610029224a283', 25, 25, null, 82, null, null, false, null),
  ('f1a90464-f1f4-5686-929e-dcba0a38d4e4', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'training', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Training is Ranger School, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Unit Armorer Course, Unit Rail/Air Loading Training Course, Basic Mountaineering Course, CBRN Officer/NCO, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), TC-AIMS, Fuel Handlers Course, Ammunition Handler, Field Sanitation Course, Drivers Training Course, Combat Lifesaver Course and Bus Driver Course, Hazardous Materials Course (OSHA). Self development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', '218160d8fed8db664fe02fe9937490d537ab515f521d923188baf806f60962f5', 25, 25, null, 83, null, null, false, null),
  ('fd716f1f-25bf-5002-9545-4f91c9d8e6ee', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'N/A.', '190a648f47ed454cf70ff2bd90dc842faae3f1fe19810cedf4bda2fbedb8201e', 26, 26, null, 84, null, null, false, null),
  ('bfccd92a-6fc8-5311-93ae-6ae6db2ee4c7', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Advanced Leader Course (ALC). Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '185cf0cef39bf056027cc04b798293332ef5e07c597deef11cb865f3781cdba7', 26, 26, null, 85, null, null, false, null),
  ('0bc72464-b35c-55d4-9fb7-a1341f75748b', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational Authorization', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'The Fire Control NCO (PLT, BTRY, BN) is the CD position at this grade. The Liaison Sergeant and Fire Control NCO (BDE, DIVARTY, EAB) are the CLT positions at this grade. These authorizations develop an NCO’s direct leadership, technical, and tactical expertise through practical application.', 'c910308252bb8dfe524ad28d06301621c0eb8feb773a44d41c7c6720233f2e6e', 26, 26, null, 86, null, null, false, null),
  ('f342e222-42d5-5ce5-bd62-3796383fbb00', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Staff Sergeants who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of Ranger School, Mission Command Digital Master Gunner (MCDMG), Battle Staff NCO Course, Drill Sergeant School, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator Course, TC-AIMS II, Unit Movement I & II, TC-AIMS System Administrator / Database Administrator, Jumpmaster School, Master Driver Trainer, Pathfinder, Common Faculty Development – Developer Course (CFD-DC), Common Faculty Development – Instructor Course (CFD-IC), Recruiting School, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Joint Counter–Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Operator, Joint Counter–Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Planner, Rappel Master, Equal Opportunity Leader Course (EOLC), Basic Mountaineering Course, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL). Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', '6bc652aa41c5a4143b444441c26af4894ebb6a301a2a4ae6987e9bda8a793adf', 26, 26, null, 87, null, null, false, null),
  ('bb1975e8-c7b2-59b9-a8e3-d5f58cd6af91', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Broadening authorizations are crucial to developing leaders with a wide range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments. These assignments include Fire Control OC/T, Drill Sergeant, Instructor, Small Group Leader (SGL), Recruiter, Training Developer, Training Management NCO, and Range Safety NCO.', 'cf4192248c2441d426b7e7b9c4cfdff6963e96e66ead4c512c2efd95af2379c8', 26, 26, null, 88, null, null, false, null),
  ('bd4e5bd5-53c3-5d09-af9a-1acb804dba08', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Senior Leader Course (SLC). Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '554afdffc42c68bacaf04179dbb79a2f1b6e30280190cdb4ceadbe9d0282a28f', 26, 26, null, 89, null, null, false, null),
  ('b171c8d1-4f8a-5e76-ad27-47a0bf8abe3d', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'The Senior Fire Control NCO (BN, BDE, DIVARTY) and Battery Operations Sergeant are the CD positions at this grade. Senior Fire Control NCO (EAB), Intelligence Sergeant and Liaison Sergeant are the CLT positions at this grade. These authorizations develop an NCO’s direct leadership, technical, and tactical expertise through practical application. The focus at this level is on the operational unit, where SFC build on their foundational knowledge to become technical and tactical experts while improving their leadership abilities.', '82243a7d627cabbbea1bdfba0dd3a9e8f2aa69eadcfebf1d4d3fc023393d326a', 26, 26, null, 90, null, null, false, null),
  ('9605739d-ef5a-510b-bbff-c79803dbce5c', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Sergeant First Class who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of FA Master Gunner Course, Mission Command Digital Master Gunner (MCDMG), Battle Staff NCO Course, Ranger School, Drill Sergeant School, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator Course, Protection Cell Operations, Protection Integration, TC-AIMS II Unit Movement I & II, TC-AIMS System Administrator / Database Administrator, Jumpmaster School, Master Driver Trainer, Force Management, Pathfinder, Rappel Master, Common Faculty Development – Developer Course (CFD-DC), Common Faculty Development – Instructor Course (CFD-IC), Recruiting School, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Joint Counter–Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Operator, Joint Counter–Small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Planner, Equal Opportunity Advisor Course (EOA), Suicide Intervention Trainer, Basic Mountaineering Course. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', '0899ba2045c635c9144efdcf213b71236e6924de4fc6f24c7432035f839c3655', 26, 27, null, 91, null, null, false, null),
  ('fc6a2d20-175a-57f6-9f29-7473a2cc093c', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13J', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 7. MOS 13J Fire Control Specialist:', 'Broadening Authorizations are crucial in developing leaders with a wide range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments. These assignments include Career Management NCO (FAPO), Career Advisor (HRC), Military Science Instructor (MSI), BN FDC NCO OC/T, BTRY FDC OC/T, Senior Drill Sergeant, Small Group Leader (SLC), Senior Instructor, Senior Small Group Leader (ALC), Training Developer, Inspector General NCO, Research Development Test and Evaluation NCO (RDTE), Training Management NCO, Sexual Assault Response Coordinator, EO Advisor, CD Staff NCO.', '1d6adf8e80290889ccd9e3b0d6a81e83a3ac07b9d202a22134443cf59bed8bb5', 27, 27, null, 92, null, null, false, null),
  ('bb389b0c-3b2e-5475-bbb6-24441be8f2eb', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'System (HIMARS) Crewmember Career Guide:', 'd90e0f193b8de1578904df0d2f07b6fce432b73cc518249f1938864fc7396056', 27, 27, null, 93, null, null, false, null),
  ('8e9de901-65e9-5d3f-b6cb-616d87a84e67', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'The primary development goal for MLRS/HIMARS Crewmembers is to become technically and tactically proficient leaders capable of executing Large-Scale Combat Operations (LSCO) in a multi-domain environment. To achieve this, Soldiers must seek and excel in career developmental leadership positions and strive for excellence while attending the NCO Professional Development System (NCOPDS) and functional courses that provide skills critical to the modern battlefield. Following mastery of core competencies, NCOs should pursue broadening assignments that provide a purposeful expansion of knowledge and skills fundamental to their continued growth and adaptability throughout the career life cycle. To ensure lethality and readiness for high-intensity conflict, Soldiers must make every effort to achieve the highest possible score on the Army Fitness Test (AFT) and weapons qualifications. Soldiers should attend military courses that expand and improve MOS competencies to advance their combat effectiveness', '313db4f15df69d739b927621a781876b5c430868adabf6970d07ffa82fcfa123', 27, 27, null, 94, null, null, false, null),
  ('312fa3cc-2b80-5c56-847f-9029b4e8097a', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'Basic Combat Training (BCT) and Advanced Individual Training (AIT). Graduating BCT/AIT with honors is one of many ways to identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '3e43f028b99b4f49d2216fd655b385214bcda7f1dda379e0ec0087d1f2acaa00', 28, 28, null, 95, null, null, false, null),
  ('39002850-9c67-5f52-862b-bd034580f819', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'MLRS/HIMARS profession is based around the core operational authorizations: Vehicle Driver, Reconnaissance Specialist, HEMTT Driver, Launcher Driver, and Ammunition Specialist. Through these hands-on assignments, the primary focus is on mastering technical expertise and basic MOS skills while gaining proficiency in critical Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills. This expertise is developed and validated through rigorous participation in unit training events, including Artillery Tables, CTC rotations, and tactical exercises, which simulate the demands of operational environments.', 'ed634845e7d57e7f35c0bdc4786273a34da00a7f1ebd15069247eb177df8171c', 28, 28, null, 96, null, null, false, null),
  ('e5a48748-f26e-5de3-a83e-0f94ff16e4b0', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Self-development', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'MLRS/HIMARS Crewmembers who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as Soldier of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Key Training is Ranger School Ammunition Handler Course, Combat Lifesaver Course, Driver Training Course, CBRN Officer/NCO, Field Sanitation Course, Fuel Handler Course, Unit Armorer Course, and Unit Rail/Air Loading Training Course. Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Bus Drivers Course, Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', 'f4785923056ca6c08fa643dd94ffc99b62bf1cb2455fba46d0f76be032b56f00', 28, 28, null, 97, null, null, false, null),
