  ('126136be-947d-5b19-ac7b-f22e30ef9d5e', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'The primary development goal for WLR specialists is to become technically and tactically proficient leaders capable of executing Large-Scale Combat Operations (LSCO) in a multidomain environment. To achieve this, Soldiers must seek and excel in career developmental leadership positions and strive for excellence while attending the NCO Professional Development System (NCOPDS) and functional courses that provide skills critical to the modern battlefield. Following mastery of core competencies, NCOs should pursue broadening assignments that provide a purposeful expansion of knowledge and skills fundamental to their continued growth and adaptability throughout the career life cycle. To ensure lethality and readiness for high-intensity conflict, Soldiers must make every effort to achieve the highest possible score on the Army Fitness Test (AFT) and weapons qualifications. Furthermore, Soldiers should attend military courses that expand and improve MOS competencies in order to advance their combat effectiveness.', 'e6ad221ffcd6b83654301b356fba5e6f1c6111d14a390f3eb1ae032083d04b00', 30, 31, null, 112, null, null, false, null),
  ('2c2faf71-0710-5946-8e88-8805167df953', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Institutional training', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Basic Combat Training (BCT) and Advanced Individual Training (AIT). Graduating BCT/AIT with honors is one of many ways to identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '3e43f028b99b4f49d2216fd655b385214bcda7f1dda379e0ec0087d1f2acaa00', 31, 31, null, 113, null, null, false, null),
  ('c468aab6-bf55-5e14-827a-4027e9816ea1', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Operational Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'The WLR specialist career is centered on one core operational authorization: WLR specialist. This focus is essential for building a deep, technical foundation in the MOS, mastering assigned equipment, and achieving proficiency in Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills. Technical and tactical expertise is forged and validated during rigorous training events, including Artillery Tables, Combat', '153b06f77030df0808a21b2d1785877b9f0cd83372eb94f643e9b3fdd1db0b80', 31, 31, null, 114, null, null, false, null),
  ('6e4734bb-db84-5fa5-947d-7a7971318f60', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Training Center (CTC) rotations, and other field exercises', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'These combined operational and training experiences culminate in the complete mastery of core MOS competencies and all tasks outlined in the Individual Critical Task List (ICTL), which together form the bedrock of unit readiness and lethality.', '53ebc1368f34d28f18ca6688104207b4ed25814f6d7cdd1d13a37078d0ee5742', 31, 31, null, 115, null, null, false, null),
  ('b633a993-54d5-5b92-b6ea-c57489d48278', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Self-development', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'WLR specialist who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as Soldier of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Key Training is Ranger School, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Unit Armorer Course, Unit Rail/Air Loading Training Course, Fuel Handlers Course, Ammunition Handler, Field Sanitation Course, Combat Lifesaver Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level 1), and Bus Driver Course. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', 'de47ed3b29c4ebdd2dd1b2d2e0c350fda9202276f993ebcc6840779e090f589b', 31, 31, null, 116, null, null, false, null),
  ('89eab12d-0964-59ca-a9d8-b74393525760', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private/Specialist — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'N/A', 'e2f79e5b60330bba4c289962231b6ba2957d0b14e7deb3110417003c79dea635', 31, 31, null, 117, null, null, false, null),
  ('b6abf173-fad5-5a52-bd25-7d9b90bb4dd8', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant: — Institutional training', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Basic Leader Course (BLC). Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '64c67c3edf7e971075aab24d6c38e65d1e32e167e275245eec340930512baf9f', 31, 31, null, 118, null, null, false, null),
  ('a815c441-3a93-57cf-8e4f-784faa46c7a5', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant: — Operational Authorization', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'The Team Chief is the Developmental position at this grade. The focus at this level is on the operational unit, where Sergeants build on their foundational knowledge to become technical and tactical experts while improving their leadership abilities. This dedicated focus is essential for achieving complete mastery of their core competencies.', '2907b4950b480a7fabcbf121b74dcbc4f59e3483e5a7f601a567d003fcbb56f2', 31, 31, null, 119, null, null, false, null),
  ('c930709d-02ce-558e-bb2e-5a8ad81ced89', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'self_development', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant: — Self-development', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Sergeants who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Key', 'a946340848989ddd2a4ac4056d37dfeeab3cd95d164911b3616610029224a283', 31, 31, null, 120, null, null, false, null),
  ('32aa778e-82c4-5ae4-937a-8b6d697fbf66', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant: — Training', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Training is Ranger, Jungle School, Arctic Soldier Course, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Unit Armorer Course, Unit Rail/Air Loading Training Course, CBRN Officer/NCO, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), TC-AIMS, Fuel Handlers Course, Ammunition Handler, Field Sanitation Course, Drivers Training Course, Combat Lifesaver Course and Bus Driver Course, Joint Counter small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Planner, Joint Counter small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Operator, Suicide Intervention Trainer. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', '3cb86a09ad75d2c70b6dfd1a32c062fecac7cc4600bef4e2c9ed40bdd7a3712c', 31, 32, null, 121, null, null, false, null),
  ('253231e4-1c87-5833-9b17-476606cb11c1', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-4..E-5', null, 'Corporal/Sergeant: — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'N/A', 'e2f79e5b60330bba4c289962231b6ba2957d0b14e7deb3110417003c79dea635', 32, 32, null, 122, null, null, false, null),
  ('49073622-7a97-5fc9-823f-3bc69c11dd35', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Advance Leader Course (ALC) Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', 'bf8181b05fae795f9bd493d2c0fbb3e5cc10efd6d4bacf8c695fc3f087c0a602', 32, 32, null, 123, null, null, false, null),
  ('b0a1bf61-0eb0-5f3a-ab99-2ba3a2091e05', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational Authorization', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'The Section Chief is the Career Developmental position at this grade. These authorizations develop NCO’s direct leadership, technical, and tactical expertise through practical application.', 'a4fd5e6ff29f7c6fb88a7483282a01ec618e0eeba635e139733134c35c5aee61', 32, 32, null, 124, null, null, false, null),
  ('19da4064-906a-56f3-b2d4-650b128af280', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Staff Sergeants who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of Ranger School, Jumpmaster School, Master Drivers Course, Jungle School, Basic Mountaineering Course, Arctic Soldier Course, Arctic Leaders Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator Course, TC-AIMS II Unit Movement I & II, TC-AIMS System Administrator/Database Administrator, Unit Movement Officer, Equal Opportunity Leaders Course (EOLC), Rappel Master, Tactical Combatives Course Level II, ACE/SI. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional', 'c4a9c81ddd90ad29c326fc9b368abbb1e5bf044455164f8cef6440e283e9b999', 32, 32, null, 125, null, null, false, null),
  ('8e2fea1e-6fb3-5cd0-bf77-098e7b0f0a5f', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Broadening authorizations are crucial to developing leaders with a wide range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments. These assignments include OC/T, Drill Sergeant, Test and Evaluation NCO, Small Group Leader (SGL), Instructor, and', 'feee3e4d8b9003fb49cb32b209a58ecc9ee7ccbb675e4b3f8ef83c7cd562d723', 32, 32, null, 126, null, null, false, null),
  ('a9781270-bc3e-5b24-ac41-9843252fec78', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Senior Leader Course (SLC). Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', '554afdffc42c68bacaf04179dbb79a2f1b6e30280190cdb4ceadbe9d0282a28f', 32, 32, null, 127, null, null, false, null),
  ('3e6160f5-5f66-5847-bb85-6ac67db9d549', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'The Platoon Sergeant and the Counterfire NCO are the CD positions at this grade. These authorizations develop an NCO’s direct leadership, technical, and tactical expertise through practical application. The focus at this level is on the operational unit, where SFC build on their foundational knowledge to become technical and tactical experts while improving their leadership abilities.', '1c279b1e226a2c523a4bbc7a36a57c344ff66c5d27f0770276a6fa470d5c1b37', 32, 32, null, 128, null, null, false, null),
  ('4f7a554c-bdc9-532c-92b7-d22a950875e8', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Sergeant First Class who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of Ranger School, FA Master Gunner Course, Battle Staff NCO Course, Mission Command Digital Master Gunner Course, Knowledge Management Qualification Course, Jumpmaster School, Master Drivers Course, Basic Mountaineering Course, Jungle School, Arctic Soldier Course, Arctic Leaders Course, Force Management, Protection Cell Operations, Protection Integration, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator Course, Security Managers Course, TC-AIMS II, and Unit Movement Officer II, Joint Counter small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Planner, Joint Counter small Unmanned Aircraft Systems (C-sUAS) Operator, Rappel Master, Tactical Combatives Course Level II. ACE/SI. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', '8aae947439c0c3c0ca14bf5c72073bd215564575eee5c4c4b9c96bebb62106a8', 32, 33, null, 129, null, null, false, null),
  ('8b45e3e1-030d-52cd-9a3f-d74936416b09', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 9. MOS 13R Weapons Locating Radar Specialist:', 'Broadening Authorizations are crucial in developing leaders with a wide range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments. These assignments include Career Management NCO (FAPO), Career Advisor NCO (HRC), Military Science Instructor (MSI), OC/T (CTC Locations), CD Staff NCO, Training Developer, Senior Small Group Leader (SSGL), Small Group Leader (SGL), OCT (AC/RC), Senior Drill Sergeant, Senior Instructor, Research Develop Test and Evaluation (RDTE), Assistant Inspector General, Recruiter, Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA).', '0028d06e3348693c3bbfcbcac4fce0c278f81a63b512181bc2d456c287e3f01d', 33, 33, null, 130, null, null, false, null),
  ('701daf7c-7822-56c9-a2ab-bb3075b785b2', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — overview', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Major duties: Master Sergeants/First Sergeants are expert leaders and managers of subordinate elements. They master and apply core competencies, unit training, and operational planning. Master Sergeants/First Sergeants possess refined leadership and advisory skills. They develop and execute solutions to readiness and tactical challenges. Prerequisites: All prerequisites are governed by the standards detailed in DA PAM 611-21. Leaders and Soldiers must refer to this publication, accessible via the Army G-1 Publications website, to ensure all requirements are met.', '9b0d384ae459d557eba96925ccf230a90270db385433b330596333dd8d45796b', 33, 33, null, 131, null, null, false, null),
  ('f8aee05f-1a9b-5f1a-bf37-43bc1e404441', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — Institutional training', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Master Leaders Course (MLC). Graduating from an NCOPDS course as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate or Commandants List will identify oneself as a top performer with significant potential.', 'db030f88c9043f35f2bccd063840595d8c38e19380e320fa75a59454b9107014', 33, 33, null, 132, null, null, false, null),
  ('d4df1c74-ab89-55a3-8d92-2e407b55c40c', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — Operational Authorizations', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'The career developmental assignment for MSGs is First Sergeant. This position qualifies MSGs to perform duties as the Senior NCO of a unit and enhances their organizational supervisory knowledge, leadership skills, and abilities. MSGs should serve successfully as a First Sergeant for at least 36 months. There is no position in the grade of MSG that provides equivalent leadership training and development. When not assigned as a unit 1SG, the MSG should seek opportunities to serve in Critical Leader Time (CLT) authorizations such as Operations Sergeant within Cannon or Rocket formations across Field Artillery Brigades and Division Artilleries (DIVARTY). Successful performance in these positions is a conditional prerequisite for consideration to SGM.', '7cc8563d94fe89d418408b814043a1c86036f7b3cc5e53f2343d516aab415598', 33, 33, null, 133, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad7b6c9b-4562-5716-aa06-38b6ed74893d', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'MSGs/1SGs should strive to develop a full understanding of combined arms, fire support operations, battalion-level staff operations and command principles. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. They should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of Ranger School, Battle Staff NCO, Jumpmaster School, Force Management, Protection Cell Operations, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator, Joint Operational Fires and Effects (JOFE), Pathfinder, Arctic Leader, Joint Air Tactical Operations, Tactical Air Operations, Observer Controller Trainer, Air Assault and Basic Airborne Course.', 'a8f39a8f3c6ab79ec9d176328290e737bd1c3e6a0c40a8cb4666b637d4016f3a', 33, 34, null, 134, null, null, false, null),
  ('6004411a-9756-52b2-9c87-14a57ab4a899', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include professional', 'ceca590a2d3c4c68297ea6e35e96c0000676e6a2f73775f92366ab80869c4b14', 34, 34, null, 135, null, null, false, null),
  ('bf499f9b-e970-51ec-b3d5-3f3dc6e23f35', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'MSG/1SG — Broadening Authorizations', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Essential for cultivating agile leaders with the diverse perspectives and multi-functional expertise required to navigate increasingly complex, high-stakes environments. Furthermore, professional education remains a pillar of career progression; MSGs must pursue advanced academic degrees and specialized technical certifications to enhance their strategic decision-making and stay ahead of evolving industry and organizational standards. These assignments include: Career Management NCO (FAPO), Senior Talent Management NCO (HRC), Senior Military Science Instructor (SMSI), Military Science Instructor (MSI), Firing BTRY HQ OC/T (Observer/ Controller/ Trainer), Deputy Commandant, Inspector General NCO, Chief Instructor, Division NCOIC, Senior Training Developer, Small Group Leader (MLC).', '1d0a46ed67e4cc4460d26c2731147d918e1865a8d8918569fa4e3ec4908c1231', 34, 34, null, 136, null, null, false, null),
  ('4c5d7f88-6ed1-55cf-bf9c-0dd3de1712ac', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — overview', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Major duties: Sergeants Major/Command Sergeants Major must be interpersonal leaders, talent managers, and team builders. They understand and employ concepts and doctrine across multiple domains (joint operations, combined arms maneuver, and joint fires). SGM/CSMs possess exceptional oral and written communication skills. They can conceptualize and devise solutions to complex problems. Prerequisites: All prerequisites are governed by the standards detailed in DA PAM 611-21. Leaders and Soldiers must refer to this publication, accessible via the Army G-1 Publications website, to ensure all requirements are met.', '366474c045134bb93d00fb37fd14ab674f17df9c695ef0a5e2d2d2efcff585c8', 34, 34, null, 137, null, null, false, null),
  ('e5a12961-42bf-56ac-9d29-5298284c3453', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Institutional Training SGM/CSM development focuses on executive leadership within the Army Leader Development Model. Sergeant Major Academy (SGM-A): Completion of the Sergeants Major Course (SMC) is the baseline for all SGMs. Command Sergeants Major Development Program (CSMDP): Mandatory for all SGMs selected for CSM to ensure readiness for battalion-level command responsibility.', '0b87c1e8e4643a8f5ef9905b16a5516bb99f01bb6634fc5a5504b7a8bc217c1d', 34, 34, null, 138, null, null, false, null),
  ('d06adc02-0168-5ccd-846f-57f3300d5cd4', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Operational Assignments While a select percentage of SGMs are chosen for Command, every SGM is a strategic asset across the Operating and Generating Forces.', '7bfa0bf67ae407076363abfc61dc43a2066f93fe4ce00e553db02d6978de25d2', 34, 34, null, 139, null, null, false, null),
  ('b59a4d77-ecfd-509e-a0e7-ffad5f946ea9', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Career Developmental (CD) SGM', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'The benchmark CD assignment is a Battalion-level Operations Sergeant Major position.', 'add250350d9ec46e7dc1772f1b36de183ffe8a1951fa7a261480353c4b1f1507', 34, 34, null, 140, null, null, false, null),
  ('1c38a1c2-c441-5312-8bea-3d45d162b19d', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Career Developmental (CSM)', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Successful performance as a Battalion Command Sergeant Major in either the Operating or Generating Force. Force Impact: All SGMs must seek professionally challenging assignments at the Battalion, Brigade, DIVARTY, and MDTF levels. They are expected to provide expert counsel to commanders and make significant contributions to the Branch’s modernization and lethality.', 'b89b0b9f325b6ba78c4ec7f08e911ee01c6cc37bfdc3be0d096134b60414b992', 34, 35, null, 141, null, null, false, null),
  ('023f90e4-bb6a-5d4e-a723-29a35d7e3d21', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Self-Development', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Self-Development SGMs must transition from technical experts to Strategic Fire Support Leaders. Education: SGMs are strongly encouraged to complete a master’s degree or higher. Multidomain Expertise: Leaders must master the entire Fires Kill Chain (Sensor, Control, and Delivery). This requires rigorous self-study of Joint Fires doctrine and the integration of emerging technologies (e.g., PRC-160 HF, Long-Range Precision Fires). Strategic Mentorship: Focus on the mastery of executive-level mentoring and the holistic development of the NCO Corps. SGMs must be the "Masters of Warfighting," capable of operating in Joint, Interagency, Intergovernmental, and Multinational (JIIM) environments.', 'b4850ae5f6da514441b76a0fb1ce88e7e1797711065c1cf41c62cba29f188ac3', 35, 35, null, 142, null, null, false, null),
  ('dd008b07-622e-58bc-a24e-a4110a75cbc9', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Additional Training', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Additional Training To maintain a competitive edge for senior-level billets, SGMs should pursue: Professional Courses: Keystone, CSM/SGM Force Management Course', '8c3774e28b222feb5520859d1d299b2ec8214a477a87532792057de82a7c23ad', 35, 35, null, 143, null, null, false, null),
  ('240f2488-3b4b-51b6-9a6a-983c2a3b2dca', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Broadening', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Broadening & Special Assignments', '2aebf74b355467302a42d7a08b7a00089054349877b16091c535922711ff7d98', 35, 35, null, 144, null, null, false, null),
  ('2790bc4f-487c-5aa2-ac67-dc68056b111f', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'SGM/CSM — Broadening', 'Chapter 10. 13Z Field Artillery Senior Sergeant/13Z Command Sergeant Major:', 'Broadening is critical to producing versatile leaders for an ever-changing global security environment. Priority assignments include: Enterprise Leadership: Army Staff Fellowships, USANCOA Instructor, or NCOA Commandant. Force Generation/Modernization: Chief Career Management NCO, CTC CSM (OC/T, OC-T), DOTD SGM, TLLM SGM, AMTC SGM, Test Directorate SGM. Joint & Specialized: CMF SGM, Joint Billets, Military Personnel Exchange Program (MPEP).', 'e4214c3f7883a199eca3766f725ef5a3ca27ecd4616511f82644421cfc01f933', 35, 35, null, 145, null, null, false, null);
